          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "JWT Algorithm Confusion / Token Forgery — Ruled out: JWT Token (RS256 algorithm)\n\nJWT tokens use RS256 (RSA Signature) algorithm with proper key binding. Tested for algorithm confusion (RS256 to HS256) which failed - server correctly validates RS256 signature using public key. No 'alg': 'none' acceptance. Token is cryptographically signed and not vulnerable to algorithm confusion attacks. However, tokens are accessible via SQLi vulnerability in login endpoint, so authentication bypass remains the primary issue."
          },
